<title>SWEDEN: SAS nine-month cargo up 20.8 pct.</title>
<headline>SAS nine-month cargo up 20.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian airline SAS said on Friday its cargo volumes rose 20.8 percent to 155,000 tonnes in the first nine months of 1996 compared to the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>Earlier this week SAS posted a profit of profit of 1.257 billion crowns before tax for the first nine months of 1996, compared to 2.145 billion a year earlier, blaming stagnating traffic revenues and higher operating costs.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
